no-mlkem: The fix
(TLS 1.3 works, but the server has no ML-KEM. The most common cause by far.)
Upgrade the TLS library. Hybrid PQ (X25519MLKEM768) ships in OpenSSL 3.5+, current BoringSSL and AWS-LC, Go 1.24+, and rustls with aws-lc-rs.

If the groups are set by hand, put X25519MLKEM768 first:

# nginx, on OpenSSL 3.5+

ssl_protocols TLSv1.2 TLSv1.3;

ssl_ecdh_curve X25519MLKEM768:X25519:prime256v1;

// Go 1.24+: the default includes X25519MLKEM768

cfg.CurvePreferences = nil

pqdoctor prints the version for the stack it detects. Every server’s lines are on Fixes by server. If you can’t upgrade, there’s the Cloudflare Tunnel fallback.

Fixes by server: nginx
(The exact config lines pqdoctor prints for nginx, Apache, HAProxy, Caddy, Node, Go, IIS, Java, mail servers, and the Cloudflare Tunnel fallback.)
nginx gets PQ from its TLS library. OpenSSL 3.5 or newer is needed (Ubuntu 25.04+, Debian 13+, or an nginx build linked against 3.5). Check with nginx -V.

ssl_protocols TLSv1.2 TLSv1.3;

ssl_ecdh_curve X25519MLKEM768:X25519:prime256v1;
